WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.977
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:06.277 --> 00:00:09.768
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.068 --> 00:00:16.505
Unit nine: First and Second Conditional. Today you will talk about real and imaginary situations.

4
00:00:16.805 --> 00:00:19.272
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:23.292
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.139
Condition.

7
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:29.032
Condition means a situation that must happen first.

8
00:00:29.617 --> 00:00:31.152
The condition is rain.

9
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:33.984
Your turn. Say: Condition.

10
00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:37.776
Condition.

11
00:00:38.517 --> 00:00:39.390
Result.

12
00:00:40.383 --> 00:00:43.021
Result means what happens because of something.

13
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:45.152
The result is a wet road.

14
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.089
Your turn. Say: Result.

15
00:00:50.933 --> 00:00:51.888
Result.

16
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.303
If.

17
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:56.130
If means used for a condition.

18
00:00:56.717 --> 00:00:58.658
If it rains, we will stay.

19
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.299
Your turn. Say: If.

20
00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:04.740
If.

21
00:01:05.483 --> 00:01:06.554
Unless.

22
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:09.085
Unless means if not.

23
00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:11.822
Unless you study, you will fail.

24
00:01:12.417 --> 00:01:14.744
Your turn. Say: Unless.

25
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:18.694
Unless.

26
00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:20.428
Probably.

27
00:01:21.417 --> 00:01:23.312
Probably means very likely.

28
00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.533
I will probably pass.

29
00:01:26.117 --> 00:01:28.548
Your turn. Say: Probably.

30
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.308
Probably.

31
00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:34.214
Imaginary.

32
00:01:35.217 --> 00:01:37.158
Imaginary means not real.

33
00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.564
An imaginary situation.

34
00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:42.605
Your turn. Say: Imaginary.

35
00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:46.619
Imaginary.

36
00:01:47.383 --> 00:01:48.013
Were.

37
00:01:49.017 --> 00:01:51.794
Were means the past of be in imaginary ifs.

38
00:01:52.383 --> 00:01:54.348
If I were you, I would study.

39
00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.941
Your turn. Say: Were.

40
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:00.662
Were.

41
00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:01.977
Would.

42
00:02:02.983 --> 00:02:05.401
Would means used for imaginary results.

43
00:02:06.017 --> 00:02:07.703
I would travel the world.

44
00:02:08.317 --> 00:02:10.667
Your turn. Say: Would.

45
00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.360
Would.

46
00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:18.736
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:21.943
Visal, what is the first conditional?

48
00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:34.003
It is if plus the present simple, then will plus a base verb. We use it for real or likely future situations, such as If it rains, we will stay at home.

49
00:02:35.117 --> 00:02:36.547
And the second conditional?

50
00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:50.624
It is if plus the past simple, then would plus a base verb. We use it for imaginary or unlikely situations, such as If I won a million dollars, I would buy a house.

51
00:02:51.717 --> 00:02:53.763
Is there anything special about were?

52
00:02:54.850 --> 00:03:03.598
In the if-clause of a second conditional we can say if I were you for all persons. Never use will or would in the if-clause.

53
00:03:04.733 --> 00:03:06.268
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:07.117 --> 00:03:12.413
Grammar focus: 1st: If plus present, will; 2nd: If plus past, would.

55
00:03:12.713 --> 00:03:13.958
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:16.510
If it rains, we will stay at home.

57
00:03:17.417 --> 00:03:20.252
If I won a million dollars, I would buy a house.

58
00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:28.169
Use if plus the present simple with will for likely futures, and if plus the past simple with would for imaginary situations.

59
00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:32.591
Be careful! Don't say: If I will win, I will travel.

60
00:03:34.533 --> 00:03:36.951
Say: If I win, I will travel.

61
00:03:37.251 --> 00:03:38.832
No will in the if-clause.

62
00:03:39.633 --> 00:03:42.332
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:44.367
What Would You Do?.

64
00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:47.398
If it rains tomorrow, the match will be cancelled.

65
00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:51.282
Sophea will pass the exam if she studies every day.

66
00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:55.311
If she won a prize, she would give some money to her village.

67
00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.845
If I were her, I would also buy new books.

68
00:03:59.833 --> 00:04:03.226
Unless she studies hard, she will not get a high score.

69
00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:08.602
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.438
If it rains, we blank at home.

71
00:04:11.738 --> 00:04:15.507
A, will stay. B, would stay. C, stayed.

72
00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:21.089
The answer is A: will stay.

73
00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:24.133
If I blank rich, I would travel.

74
00:04:24.433 --> 00:04:27.286
A, will be. B, were. C, am.

75
00:04:30.833 --> 00:04:32.508
The answer is B: were.

76
00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:35.394
Which is a second conditional?

77
00:04:35.694 --> 00:04:41.646
A, If it rains, we stay.. B, If you heat ice, it melts.. C, If I had wings, I would fly..

78
00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.523
The answer is C: If I had wings, I would fly..

79
00:04:49.683 --> 00:04:51.311
'Unless' means blank.

80
00:04:51.611 --> 00:04:55.009
A, if not. B, because. C, although.

81
00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:00.822
The answer is A: if not.

82
00:05:01.983 --> 00:05:04.273
What would Sophea do if she won a prize?

83
00:05:04.573 --> 00:05:08.888
A, sleep. B, give money to her village. C, buy a car.

84
00:05:12.433 --> 00:05:15.640
The answer is B: give money to her village.

85
00:05:16.833 --> 00:05:19.938
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:20.783 --> 00:05:23.108
What would you do if you won a prize?

87
00:05:31.917 --> 00:05:33.371
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:33.671 --> 00:05:45.207
If I won a prize, I would share some money with my family. I would also buy books and a laptop for school. If I studied harder every day, I could win a scholarship.

89
00:05:45.507 --> 00:05:47.286
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:48.183 --> 00:05:55.712
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and 1st: if plus present, will; 2nd: if plus past, would.

91
00:05:56.012 --> 00:05:59.848
Today's value is foresight. Prepare today for the world of tomorrow.

92
00:06:00.148 --> 00:06:02.592
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

93
00:06:02.892 --> 00:06:05.382
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

